1
00:00:03,644 --> 00:00:13,465
Start with Architecture: one unit is 30 centimetres.
Use a half-unit grid for the partitions.

2
00:00:13,515 --> 00:00:27,507
Draw the slab, forty-two by
eighteen metres: 140 by 60 units.

3
00:00:27,557 --> 00:00:46,507
Build one six metre square frame. Four corner
columns come first, using Cuboid and axis helpers.

4
00:01:42,379 --> 00:01:59,889
Nice. Add the beams at the column tops. Twelve
units overall gives a height of 3.6 metres.

5
00:03:13,373 --> 00:03:29,443
Window-select the frame and Make Object. Then
Edit Prototype to define its array handle.

6
00:03:32,079 --> 00:03:40,769
Place the hotspot above the second grid diagonal,
on an axis helper. Choose Multiply Volumetric.

7
00:03:40,819 --> 00:03:51,768
Attach every beam and column. Pick Reference
at the far corner of the first six metre bay.

8
00:03:51,818 --> 00:04:06,337
Good. Select the instance and drag its
hotspot to the opposite corner of the slab.

9
00:04:06,387 --> 00:04:15,727
Twenty-one structural modules: seven across and
three deep, all driven by one instance hotspot.

10
00:04:19,378 --> 00:04:25,598
For the core stairs, set flight height to
six units and the step count to twelve.

11
00:04:25,648 --> 00:04:38,087
Draw a rectangular contour C and Make Object,
so the same outline can define both flights.

12
00:04:38,137 --> 00:04:54,767
Add helpers for the contour copy and the landing.
Copy the contour six units across and up.

13
00:05:08,411 --> 00:05:27,041
Nice. Draw walking path P in the lower outline.
Set C, then P, to create twelve risers.

14
00:05:28,156 --> 00:05:41,961
Use the landing helpers at six units:
half the 3.6 metre storey height.

15
00:05:42,011 --> 00:05:58,961
Reverse the walking path in the upper contour,
then set C and P for the return flight.

16
00:06:01,786 --> 00:06:09,065
Hide Objects in the selection filters while drafting
the core, to keep the floor grid accessible.

17
00:06:09,115 --> 00:06:24,801
Select both flights and the landing. Move Copy
places the second evacuation stair in the east bay.

18
00:06:24,851 --> 00:06:32,671
Set partition thickness to half a unit: fifteen
centimetres. The offset is a quarter unit.

19
00:06:32,721 --> 00:06:47,431
Draw the two lift cases on the
left of the central lift hall.

20
00:07:09,540 --> 00:07:25,690
Move Copy repeats the partition assembly on the
right: four lift cases around one shared hall.

21
00:07:25,773 --> 00:07:41,173
Good. Parallel partitions separate the stair
enclosures from their outer side halls.

22
00:08:19,587 --> 00:08:38,057
Enclose the stair bays at north and south.
The middle hall remains open at both ends.

23
00:09:11,838 --> 00:09:28,096
To the west, divide the service bay into women's
and men's toilets, accessed from the side hall.

24
00:10:06,201 --> 00:10:22,315
To the east, put storage and copying north of
the kitchen, then a meeting room in the end bay.

25
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:32,390
Cut the lift openings on the wall faces.
Axis helpers carry their 2.1 metre heads.

26
00:12:57,506 --> 00:13:11,576
Give each toilet its own door from the west side hall.

27
00:13:48,646 --> 00:14:04,316
Good. Add doors between the side halls and
the two protected staircase enclosures.

28
00:14:40,435 --> 00:14:56,425
Storage and kitchen open from the east hall;
the copier room connects through storage.

29
00:16:00,004 --> 00:16:14,864
Door fits the first lift opening: ninety
centimetres wide and 2.1 metres high.

30
00:16:14,914 --> 00:16:32,744
Move Copy repeats that door. Use matching
floor-grid references in the clear open space.

31
00:18:06,612 --> 00:18:21,322
The meeting room gets a wider
entrance from the north open space.

32
00:18:47,570 --> 00:19:04,360
The east and west sides are plain walls, one
unit thick: thirty centimetres, with no windows.

33
00:19:12,961 --> 00:19:33,671
Label axes A to H and rows one to
four. Each bay is six metres square.

34
00:20:29,252 --> 00:20:47,962
Mark the lift and stair enclosures FR90,
and the side halls FR30, following the plan.

35
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:39,060
Keep the north and south bands as open offices,
connected around this central service core.

36
00:23:42,711 --> 00:23:59,661
Show Objects and lock the labels. On a quarter-unit
grid, build two mullions with no top rail.

37
00:24:26,667 --> 00:24:41,996
Join their inner corners with a closed
Polyline. The glazing fills the full height.

38
00:24:54,541 --> 00:25:11,929
Make Object, and Edit Prototype. This
panel is one and a half metres wide.

39
00:25:11,979 --> 00:25:28,769
Add a Multiply Linear hotspot, attach the panel,
and pick a reference one panel width back.

40
00:25:29,389 --> 00:25:39,399
Nice. Drag the instance handle across
the frontage: twenty-eight glazed panels.

41
00:25:39,449 --> 00:25:55,519
Move the assembled curtain wall onto the
south edge, using its corner and a helper.

42
00:25:59,704 --> 00:26:18,494
Copy the wall to the north edge. Both facades
share one definition. Then unlock the labels.

43
00:26:25,543 --> 00:26:41,212
For the ceiling, make one reusable sixty
centimetre square panel in the open office zone.

44
00:26:41,262 --> 00:26:57,572
Edit Prototype. A volumetric array hotspot
repeats the panel in both plan directions.

45
00:27:00,125 --> 00:27:16,835
Drag the instance handle to form two rows of
twenty panels, then lift the assembly on a helper.

46
00:27:36,238 --> 00:27:49,630
Good. Seven by three structural bays, four lifts, two
staircases and open offices around one central core.

47
00:27:49,680 --> 00:28:02,573
The partial ceiling leaves the layout visible. The
structural and facade grids remain hotspot-driven.
